# Test fixtures are inputs to the suite, not captured data. The extension rules above would otherwise
# keep them out of a fresh checkout, and the `include_str!` sites that read them would fail to
# compile in CI (`crates/census-crawl/src/athleticlive/tests.rs`).
!crates/*/tests/fixtures/**
!xtask/tests/fixtures/**

/saved_pages/
*.zip
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.tmp-*
/athletic_matcher
/local/
/.worktrees/
/alpha.toml
/alpha.local.toml
/playwright/.auth/
**/storage-state.json
/storage-state.json
/tmp/alpha-contract/
/node_modules/
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/
/fuzz/corpus/
!/fuzz/corpus/workbook_ingestion/seed-valid.xlsx
!/fuzz/corpus/xlsx_zip_stream/seed-valid.xlsx
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/rust_out
/mutants.out/

# Source research: reports, schemas, coverage and manifests are tracked; raw captured payloads are
# re-fetchable evidence and stay on disk only (they are what fills `fixtures/` once an adapter
# lands). 26 Python probe scripts that produced the captures were moved out of the repository
# (owner decision: zero Python in the repo) to
# ~/Downloads/midwest-tfxc-source-research/repo-probes/.
research/sources/**/samples/*
!research/sources/**/samples/*.md
*.curlerr
